%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 51f1835016ff0a34f94d5a8c060c9cdd, type: 3}
  m_Name: Instructions
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  instructions:
  - name: Hello
    sprite: {fileID: 8398557208487646791, guid: 068559f04df911c4b98f00f15e86aa7e, type: 2}
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 16fba6d30ed741d4a9fdd6e79ee2f3ac, type: 3}
    instructionText: Hello, today you are going to learn how does a mechanical watch
      work and will actually assemble one.
    nextStageConditions:
      timeToNextStage: 5
      onGrabObjectName: 
      onDropObjectName: 
      onSnapObjectName: 
  - name: The Basics
    sprite: {fileID: 409948387602054397, guid: 2dbd778585cad2044ad141aa1f7e172b, type: 2}
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 16fba6d30ed741d4a9fdd6e79ee2f3ac, type: 3}
    instructionText: First things first, try and grab that ball in front of you.
      If you grab it with your both hands you can also scale it as you wish.
    nextStageConditions:
      timeToNextStage: 0
      onGrabObjectName: Ball
      onDropObjectName: 
      onSnapObjectName: 
  - name: Scalling
    sprite: {fileID: 8398557208487646791, guid: 068559f04df911c4b98f00f15e86aa7e, type: 2}
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b319a2e4ff8f5d840b82d8635b645d22, type: 3}
    instructionText: Great now grab it with both hands and make it bigger or smaller.
    nextStageConditions:
      timeToNextStage: 0
      onGrabObjectName: Ball
      onDropObjectName: 
      onSnapObjectName: 
  - name: throw it away
    sprite: {fileID: 409948387602054397, guid: 2dbd778585cad2044ad141aa1f7e172b, type: 2}
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 16fba6d30ed741d4a9fdd6e79ee2f3ac, type: 3}
    instructionText: Great Job, now throw it away to start assembling the watch
    nextStageConditions:
      timeToNextStage: 0
      onGrabObjectName: 
      onDropObjectName: Ball
      onSnapObjectName: 
  - name: Intro
    sprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 7461125ec591a1548883bd61123e9138, type: 3}
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b319a2e4ff8f5d840b82d8635b645d22, type: 3}
    instructionText: Right now you have the main plate in front of you and some of
      the gears on the right. Take some time to find them all!!
    nextStageConditions:
      timeToNextStage: 0
      onGrabObjectName: 
      onDropObjectName: 
      onSnapObjectName: 
  - name: The Main Plate
    sprite: {fileID: 5597866820062511089, guid: b67720d903bde5348a251d146c89d5d5, type: 2}
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b319a2e4ff8f5d840b82d8635b645d22, type: 3}
    instructionText: The Main Plate is the biggest , yellow piece , we will be aligning
      all the other pieces on it . You can try and play with it a little bit.
    nextStageConditions:
      timeToNextStage: 10
      onGrabObjectName: 
      onDropObjectName: 
      onSnapObjectName: 
  - name: The Barrel
    sprite: {fileID: -8370015614666040204, guid: 370ba82b73d44544aaf452de14c4ef4d, type: 2}
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b319a2e4ff8f5d840b82d8635b645d22, type: 3}
    instructionText: The Barrel is the RED GEAR. Pleasse take a minute to find it
      and grab it
    nextStageConditions:
      timeToNextStage: 0
      onGrabObjectName: GearRed
      onDropObjectName: 
      onSnapObjectName: 
  - name: The Barrel
    sprite: {fileID: 10916, guid: 0000000000000000f000000000000000, type: 0}
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b319a2e4ff8f5d840b82d8635b645d22, type: 3}
    instructionText: Great! The piece you are holding is called the barrel. It's
      the heart of the Watch and it is the only piece that moves itself.
    nextStageConditions:
      timeToNextStage: 6
      onGrabObjectName: 
      onDropObjectName: 
      onSnapObjectName: 
  - name: The Barrel
    sprite: {fileID: -8370015614666040204, guid: 370ba82b73d44544aaf452de14c4ef4d, type: 2}
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b319a2e4ff8f5d840b82d8635b645d22, type: 3}
    instructionText: Great! The piece you are holding is called the barrel. It's
      the heart of the Watch and it is the only piece that moves itself.
    nextStageConditions:
      timeToNextStage: 6
      onGrabObjectName: 
      onDropObjectName: 
      onSnapObjectName: 
  - name: The Barrel
    sprite: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 9430f133ccdfa5e408338d568da2827d, type: 3}
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b319a2e4ff8f5d840b82d8635b645d22, type: 3}
    instructionText: The Movement happens because of a string inside of it that is
      always pushing it on the sides and forcing it to move.
    nextStageConditions:
      timeToNextStage: 6
      onGrabObjectName: 
      onDropObjectName: 
      onSnapObjectName: 
  - name: The Barrel
    sprite: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 9430f133ccdfa5e408338d568da2827d, type: 3}
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b319a2e4ff8f5d840b82d8635b645d22, type: 3}
    instructionText: Normally a Barrel has around 14.000 rotations saved up, wich
      means that every watch should stop working after 4 Hours. Not really useful
      right?
    nextStageConditions:
      timeToNextStage: 6
      onGrabObjectName: 
      onDropObjectName: 
      onSnapObjectName: 
  - name: Gears
    sprite: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 9430f133ccdfa5e408338d568da2827d, type: 3}
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b319a2e4ff8f5d840b82d8635b645d22, type: 3}
    instructionText: So now we will learn how to make it rotate a lot more. Please
      put the Barrel in a comfortble place for you and grab the Brown Gear.
    nextStageConditions:
      timeToNextStage: 0
      onGrabObjectName: GearBrown
      onDropObjectName: 
      onSnapObjectName: 
  - name: Multiply Rotations.
    sprite: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 9430f133ccdfa5e408338d568da2827d, type: 3}
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b319a2e4ff8f5d840b82d8635b645d22, type: 3}
    instructionText: Try and connect the brown Gear to the Barrel. You will obesrve
      that the brown one rotates much faster, and the smaller the gear the faster
      it rotates, that's exactly the way we are going to multiplicate the batery-life
    nextStageConditions:
      timeToNextStage: 10
      onGrabObjectName: 
      onDropObjectName: 
      onSnapObjectName: 
  - name: Assembly The Watch
    sprite: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 9430f133ccdfa5e408338d568da2827d, type: 3}
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b319a2e4ff8f5d840b82d8635b645d22, type: 3}
    instructionText: Now that we understand what those pieces are, how about we try
      and place the existing pieces at the right place on the MainPlate?
    nextStageConditions:
      timeToNextStage: 0
      onGrabObjectName: 
      onDropObjectName: 
      onSnapObjectName: 
